      "description": "Watch irense vs SC Braga highlights and goals from Primeira Liga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 9, 2026. The Primeira Liga action intensified on August 9, 2026 , as irense and SC Braga met in a fixture that promised tactical intrigue and high energy. Both sides looked to assert their dominance from the opening whistle in a match that kept the spectators on the edge of their seats throughout both halves. A Lightning Exchange of Goals The contest exploded into life within the first ten minutes, featuring a rapid-fire exchange that set a frantic tone. SC Braga drew first blood in the 7th minute when Fran Navarro found the back of the net with a clinical left-footed finish, assisted by Carvalho . The home fans didn't have to wait long for a response, however; just one minute later, Nile John produced a moment of magic for irense , unleashing a strike from outside the box that beat the keeper to level the score at 1-1. As the first half progressed, the game settled into a more physical battle. Yellow cards were issued to Diogo Travassos and Guilherme Liberato as both teams fought for control of the midfield. Despite several corner opportunities for both sides, clear-cut chances remained at a premium, and the teams headed into the locker rooms with the deadlock unbroken. Braga Assumes Control The second half saw tactical adjustments from both benches, but it was SC Braga who initially reaped the rewards. In the 66th minute, substitute Pau Victor made his mark on the game. Assisted by Demir Tiknaz , Victor struck a right-footed shot that restored the visitors' lead. Braga dominated possession for much of the period, keeping the ball for 64% of the match and looking likely to see out the result as the clock ticked toward the 90th minute. Stoppage Time Heroics Just as the game seemed to be slipping away from the hosts, irense orchestrated a stunning comeback in the dying moments. In the first minute of stoppage time, Joao Veloso unleashed a powerful long-range effort that flew into the net, assisted by a cross from Gilberto Batista . The stadium held its breath as a VAR check for a potential goal was conducted, but the referee eventually signaled that the goal would stand. The final minutes were marked by desperation and rising tempers. Pau Victor received a yellow card for unsportsmanlike conduct, and despite SC Braga 's late attempts to manufacture a winner, the referee blew the final whistle. The match concluded as a hard-fought draw, leaving both sides with a point after a dramatic evening of football."
